Tauri CLI pinned in desktop/bun.lock is 2.12.0; the official matching source
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tauri-apps/tauri/tauri-cli-v2.12.0/crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/windows/nsis/installer.nsi
writes the InstallLocation registry value with literal surrounding quotes.
Our test previously passed this value directly to Test-Path. On PowerShell
7.5.4 locally, Test-Path of a quoted existing directory returned False while
the unquoted directory returned True. This is a strong hypothesis consistent
with the failure, but the actual registry value was not captured in that run.
The fix removes one balanced enclosing quote pair, rejects malformed/internal
quotes, retains empty-location fallback and every existing Test-Path, exact
binary, authenticated sidecar and uninstall assertion. Quote, plain, fallback,
malformed input and existing negative/auth controls: 13 pass/0 fail. Entire
release suite: 325 pass/0 fail locally. Native Windows rerun is essential.
